Disliked by all beings, miserable as well as diseased, / he obtains a deformed appearance, tainted by his own karma;
a hater of gods and brahmins, excluded from all observances, / completely devoid of all dharma, bereft of the conduct of the virtuous; / lacking reverence, ill-behaved, eating foul food, censuring brahmins, / not visiting sacred fords or temples of gods, devoid of the svadhā call and blessings;
